WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.640
Rarely do the giants of Dark Souls have happy fates.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.360
In the Age of the Gods, they had it best.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:11.060
Perhaps because one of their own was a powerful knight of Gwyn.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.780
Yet, even then, he suffered at the hands of former humans,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:20.660
who packed his helm with tree resin, and fooled him into thinking he was blind.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:25.080
The other giants of this Age were put to use as basic laborers.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:30.260
Their wits made them unfit for much else, except in rare occasions.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:35.780
In Drangleic, a distant race of giants invade the kingdom of the humans

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:38.480
to take back that which was stolen from them.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.300
It ends in bloodshed.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:43.640
Not to mention the giants taken for experimentation,

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.620
their very souls becoming displaced from their bodies.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:52.900
And finally, Lothric, where their abuse hits new heights.

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:54.300
Imprisoned,

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.560
forced to wallow in the muck of the cathedral,

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.760
slaughtered, or feigning death.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.880
Only one rose above the rest, and even ruled over humans:

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:07.740
Yhorm.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:11.380
Yhorm is the descendant of an ancient conqueror,

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:16.040
a conqueror who once subdued the people of the Profaned Capitol.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.360
And in time, Yhorm was asked by these very same people to lead them.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:23.860
He would come to accept this role,

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:28.600
and he served as both their weighty blade, and their stone-hard shield.

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:35.160
And you would think this transfer of power would earn him the people's respect and gratitude.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:36.840
But it didn't.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:42.680
Instead, those who spoke of Yhorm as "Lord" were quite insincere.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.640
Perhaps this is because of Yhorm's heritage.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:51.200
We don't know who the conqueror before Yhorm was,

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:54.440
and he might not even be featured in-game.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:58.020
Our two biggest clues, however, are Yhorm's size,

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:03.900
and the fact that the people of the Capitol suddenly found themselves without a ruler or protector,

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.460
and needed to ask for one.

00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:09.060
And, in my opinion, Wolnir,

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:13.820
the enormous conqueror of Carthus, who suddenly fell to the Abyss,

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.860
fits this criteria.

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:18.520
Or at least, is a good example of it.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.180
Wolnir once brought the rightful lords of the world to their knees,

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.440
and ground their crowns to dust.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.700
However, he went on to fall to the Abyss,

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.940
presumably leaving many kingdoms without a ruler.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.920
And Wolnir wasn't exactly known for sharing his power with others.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:41.240
So, at the very least it was probably an absence of rule, like this,

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:45.440
that lead the people of the capital to ask for a powerful protector

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.160
instead of simply being conquered all over again.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.720
So it fits, that they would ask Yhorm,

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.440
yet it also fits that they would feel some shame for having to ask him.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.200
Their fate would be in the hands of the conqueror's descendant.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.840
And not just that, but in the hands of a giant no less.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.300
Simpletons, and dullards with very few notable exceptions.

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:13.340
So Yhorm fought hard to prove himself as lord, risking everything for his people.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:17.080
Against the kingdom's enemies he fought unflinchingly,

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:20.380
Great Machete in one hand and greatshield in the other.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:26.700
Yet, still, his people's shame and prejudice must have manifested as bitterness,

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:27.560
distrust,

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:28.820
For...

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:31.220
In another brave gesture,

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.420
Yhorm gave his people the means to defeat him.

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.360
A Storm Ruler.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.620
An ancient sword also known as "Giant Slayer."

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:45.960
Capable of bringing giants to their knees from the strength of storm held within it.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:51.480
Yhorm carried two of these and now, only one remained in his possession.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:58.020
At some point, during the wars, Yhorm lost the one he wished to protect.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.380
It's not clear who this is...

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:02.940
Whether they were a friend or a partner,

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.380
nor how they died.

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:08.700
But, this loss became the legacy of his later years.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:12.540
It was an event so significant he threw away his greatshield,

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:16.080
for he was no longer interested in self-preservation,

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.200
nor the protection of others.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:24.920
In the place of his shield, Yhorm added a left-handed notch to his machete,

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:29.740
enabling the smashing technique of a berserker with nothing left to lose.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.840
In time, his enemies were crushed,

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:36.420
and the only threat to the capital was from within.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:41.620
The group of women, relatives of some oracle from a by-gone age,

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:45.480
suddenly triggered a curse subsisting deep within them.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.120
They all distorted into the same monstrosity,

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:55.100
an enormous hand with calcified protrusions and a hole swelling deep within the palm.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:57.320
Despite all of this,

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:00.040
they went of living without any cares,

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:05.620
and from that day forward, the Profaned Flame was born within the capitol.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.100
The Profaned Flame...

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:10.540
It came to define the capitol.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:13.500
And it was defined by three rules:

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:14.520
One:

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:17.140
It is said to be in-extinguishable.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:18.040
Two:

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.860
It is able to swallow the hearts of those it touches,

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.640
inspiring cruelty, and torture.

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:25.680
And three:

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:29.020
The darkness of the Abyss can be seen within it.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:35.720
With nothing left to lose, and a monumental soul to burn, Yhorm decided to link the fire.

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.160
With this act, he would put the Profaned Flame to rest,

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:43.880
enable a new age of fire, and prove his detractors wrong.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:46.600
Show them all they were wrong about him.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:48.480
So,

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:52.480
just as he gave one Storm Ruler to those who doubted him,

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:55.000
he gave the other to one that he trusted...

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.080
Along with a promise.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:01.840
That Siegward, this bumbling, kind-hearted knight of Catarina,

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:05.600
would slay his old friend if he ever faltered in his duty.

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.440
And so the fire was linked.

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.140
And... Yhorm failed.

00:06:11.780 --> 00:06:13.560
In all the ways that they said he would...

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:21.140
In this place we get an unprecedented look into the linking of the fire.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.800
When it happened, items say,

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.520
"A rush of flame fell from the sky,

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:30.100
and incinerated not only Yhorm...

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.380
But all the residents of the capitol."

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:35.920
So, the question, we're left asking is,

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:37.400
was this normal?

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:40.640
Or, was Yhorm's soul somehow not enough?

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.600
Were giants not supposed to link the fire?

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:46.680
For all his hard work protecting these people...

00:06:46.900 --> 00:06:48.340
They all went up in flames,

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:53.800
and I assume his detractors would have felt validated in doubting Yhorm.

00:06:53.900 --> 00:06:56.220
If they weren't all burnt to crisp.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:07:01.360
Ages pass, bolstered, in part, by Yhorm's sacrifice.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:06.880
But, the fire inevitably fades and Yhorm is brought back from the dead,

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:08.820
to link the fire once more.

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:15.840
There must be something about a second chance at life that causes a lord to fear death.

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:19.420
For, like the other two lords that rose alongside him,

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:25.160
Yhorm flees his duty and settles in the ruined capitol he once called home.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:32.680
He takes his old throne, which is now surrounded by the melted corpses of those who once doubted him,

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:34.320
and.. He waits..

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:38.560
Truly alone this time even more so than he was in life

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:41.060
Moment

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.860
Has almost come

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:45.700
I just need a bit more time

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:50.760
Seigward with a little help from you of course

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:53.620
Finds the courage to meet his old friend

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:05.940
Yhorm

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:07.960
Old friend

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:15.680
I... Siegward of the knights of Catarina

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:18.540
Have come to uphold my promise

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:26.600
Let the sun shine upon this lord of cinder

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:46.160
(Gasping)

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:51.180
It seems... I am in your debt once again

00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:53.440
My thanks

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.800
I could have not kept my promise without you

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:58.700
Now

00:08:58.980 --> 00:09:00.380
For a final toast

00:09:03.820 --> 00:09:04.960
To your valor

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.400
And my old friend Yhorm

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:12.060
Long may the sun shine

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:15.360
Ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha haaaaa

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:16.220
ha

00:09:17.420 --> 00:09:17.920
Well

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:20.760
I'm going to have myself a little nap

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:23.960
The only thing to do really after a nice toast

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:26.280
You are a true friend

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:28.900
Best of luck with you duty

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:31.880
After your final toast

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.760
As you leave the arena

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.260
Seigward's soul floats toward you

00:09:40.020 --> 00:09:43.060
Did he die from wounds that he sustained during the fight

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:45.660
Its impossible you'd think

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:47.780
Considering that Seigbro has

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:49.360
Healing properties

00:09:49.760 --> 00:09:50.260
No

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.480
His quest is complete

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:54.140
His oath is fulfilled

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.900
So Seigward ends his life

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:57.680
For all that remained

00:09:57.680 --> 00:09:59.200
Was that final toast

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.480
And to wish you luck

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:01.440
With your duty

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:03.980
In the end

00:10:04.460 --> 00:10:06.880
All that came form the Profaned Capitol

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:08.580
Were the cinders of a lord

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:11.480
Fit only to surrender its fire

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:13.020
For your ambition

00:10:13.620 --> 00:10:16.580
So knowing all of this and all of what happened

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:18.320
What do you make of it

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:22.040
Oh and did I forget to mention

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:24.080
The Profaned Flame burns on

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:26.080
Exempt from the tragedy and

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.400
Waiting for more hearts to corrupt

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:30.140
And somewhere

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:32.540
A young sorcerer escapes a painting

